AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_63916> "A carbobicyclic compound that is prostaglandin I<small><sub>2</sub></small> in which the endocyclic oxygen is replaced by a methylene group and in which the (1<i>E</i>,3<i>S</i>)-3-hydroxyoct-1-en-1-yl side chain is replaced by a (3<i>R</i>)-3-hydroxy-4-methyloct-1-en-6-yn-1-yl group. A synthetic analogue of prostacyclin, it is used as the trometamol salt (generally by intravenous infusion) for the treatment of peripheral vascular disease and pulmonary hypertension.")
